check out the `src/lib.rs` page.

instead of adding everything to the body and setting `display: none` on elements,
for each of the 4 stages / views (decision, host, guest, log/chat), remove the body as it currently is,
and fill it again from scratch with inline html.

Let's start of with the decision page.

Here's an example for a function that should be called `render_decision_page`:

```
<body>
    <h2>Choose your role</h2>

    <p>This application establishes a peer-to-peer connection between two users. You can choose to be the host or the guest.</p>

    <div>
        <button id="host_selection">Host</button>
        <button id="guest_selection">Guest</button>
    </div>
</body>
```

```
#decision div {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
}
#decision button {
    margin: 1rem 1rem;
    width: 30%;
}
h2 {
    margin-top: 6rem;
}
p {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
}
button {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: 'Lucida Console', monospace;
    padding: 0.5rem;

    background-color: #f0f0f0;
    border: 1px solid;
    width: 20%;
}
```

after this we shouldn't have any global HTML and CSS anymore.

i want to pass the lambdas `on_host_decision` and `on_guest_decision` to the decision page, that get called, depending on which button the user clicks. After a click, the body is removed again.